# Physicochemical Properties Analysis

## Overview

Physicochemical property analysis is a preliminary step in protein structure prediction that evaluates the physical and chemical 
characteristics of a protein from its amino acid sequence. In this project, ExPASy ProtParam was used to calculate properties that aid 
in protein characterization and structural analysis.

## Objective

To determine the physicochemical properties of the target protein and assess its stability before structure prediction.

## Methodology

The protein sequence in FASTA format was analyzed using ExPASy ProtParam to calculate key physicochemical parameters.

## Input

* Protein sequence (FASTA).

## Output

* Molecular weight.
* Theoretical pI.
* Amino acid composition.
* Instability index.
* Aliphatic index.
* GRAVY score.

## Applications

* Protein characterization.
* Stability assessment.
* Support for protein structure prediction.

## Files Included

* Protein sequence (FASTA).
* ProtParam results.

## Conclusion

The analysis provided important physicochemical properties of the target protein, offering insights into its stability and biochemical 
characteristics to support subsequent protein structure prediction.

